COMMIT: 37caef0 at 2025-10-29 14:05:13 - docs: STRATEGIC DECISION - Weight Tracker as North Star Architecture

## Major Strategic Pivot

**Decision:** Focus 100% on perfecting Weight Tracker, NOT fixing other 4 trackers

**Rationale:**
- Other trackers (Fasting, Sleep, Hydration, Mood) will be REBUILT using Weight as blueprint
- Don't waste 44 hours fixing code that will be deleted
- Weight Tracker already has proper MVVM architecture
- Industry best practice: "Don't refactor legacy - build new, sunset old"

## Revised Phase 1 Plan

**OLD PLAN (Rejected):**
- Fix all 5 managers thread safety (72 hours)
- Write tests for all 5 managers

**NEW PLAN (Approved):**
- Perfect Weight Tracker only (28 hours / 3.5 days)
- Create North Star Architecture Guide
- Leave other 4 trackers as-is (will rebuild post-beta)

**Time Saved:** 44 hours (61% reduction)

## Phase 1 Tasks (Weight Tracker Only)

1. Task 1A: Thread Safety (8 hours)
   - ThreadSafeUserDefaults wrapper
   - WeightManager migration
   - Actor-based observer suppression

2. Task 1B: Comprehensive Testing (12 hours)
   - WeightManager test suite
   - 6 ViewModel test suites
   - Coordinator tests
   - Target: 70%+ coverage

3. Task 1C: North Star Documentation (4 hours)
   - Architecture guide for rebuilding trackers
   - Code comments marking exemplary patterns
   - Templates for future rebuilds

4. Task 1D: Device Validation (4 hours)
   - Functional testing
   - Stress testing
   - Performance testing

## Known Issues (Accepted Trade-Offs)

- Other 4 trackers have thread safety violations
- Data corruption risk remains in legacy trackers
- Beta testing focuses on Weight Tracker as most stable
- All will be rebuilt in Phase 5+ using Weight blueprint

